    {
      "id": "void/return",
      "type": "void",
      "position": "method_return",
      "method": "doVoid",
      "args": [],
      "expect": true,
      "tags": [
        "nominal"
      ],
      "why": "both providers now answer the JSON literal true, so the divergence is CLOSED. It was never a disagreement about void — the Rust backend had no void arm, so `-> void` (which parses as Named(\"void\"), not a builtin) fell to the catch-all and returned JSON null. null is the failure token on the Qt slot above, so core_service reported METHOD_FAILED for a call that had in fact run. Converged in the shared cdylib glue, which now derives the void-method set from the same contract both backends compile, so a third language cannot re-open it. Honest residual: `true` is a fabricated value — indistinguishable from a real `-> bool` returning true — and null-as-failure survives untouched underneath. See known.json."
    },
