      "position": "method_arg",
      "method": "echoInt",
      "args": [
        3.7
      ],
      "expect": {
        "__error__": "dispatch_failed"
      },
      "tags": [
        "hostile"
      ],
      "why": "both providers now REJECT a fractional value for an `int`, so the divergence is CLOSED. The C++ side used to answer 3: `.get<int64_t>()` TRUNCATES a float rather than throwing. Same root cause and same fix as hostile/uint/negative — the scalar decoder bypassed the codec that every composite already went through."
