      "why": "`raw: true` means BOTH the argument and the return are observed as data: the driver passes decode_bytes=False so the python client does not materialize the tag on the way back. What this cell proves is that an `any` slot carries the canonical tagged form through the whole system untouched — on EVERY consumer, the Qt-typed ones included. It does NOT prove the collision is harmless: it is green here because on an `any` slot the map -> QByteArray -> map transformation is its own inverse, so the cell cannot see it. The lossy half is the sibling adversarial/{tstr:any}/_bytes-key, where the slot is typed. See known.json M3 under `xfail`."
